  "claim_scope": "GT-1 SAE-variant preflight: reusable ReLU/L1, TopK, Gated, JumpReLU, planted-dictionary, feature-AUC, and decoder-steering toy contracts are kept for learner exercises, then a pinned Pythia-70M-deduped checkpoint is loaded on CUDA. The report trains a 256-feature TopK-16 SAE on safe generated final-token hidden states, validates held-out normalized reconstruction against a zero baseline, checks a permuted-decoder negative control, requires nondegenerate sparse density, records held-out feature-label AUC, and tests that adding a learned decoder vector moves the matching decoder-projection score more than an orthogonal random direction. No individual SAE feature cleanly separates the labels on train or on the topic-disjoint held-out set, and this is retained as an explicit negative result. This is a local SAE mechanics preflight, not a full GPT-2/Gemma SAE benchmark or a semantic feature-interpretation claim.",
